  "gaps": [
    "The capture includes several programs (end of a prior program's concentrations, B.S. Occupational Safety and Health, M.S. Criminal Justice Administration, and a truncated M.S. Emergency Services Management); this ledger assumes the intended program is B.S. Occupational Safety and Health.",
    "The Open Electives block is printed as a range (21 – 33). The ledger uses 33 for the no-concentration path (30 + 39 + 18 + 33 = 120). If an optional 12-credit concentration is completed, open electives drop to 21.",
    "The optional concentration options are not itemized in this ledger: Construction Safety, Energy and Land Use Management, Fire Science, Industrial Hygiene, Maritime Safety, Oil and Gas, and Sustainability, each 12 credits.",
    "The degree program upper-level requirements mentioned under Open Electives are not stated in the capture.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit requirement is stated in the capture.",
    "Per-course credits for the required Natural Sciences courses (BIO 1301, CHM 1301, PHY 1301) are not printed; only the 9-credit block total is given.",
    "Approved course lists for Social and Behavioral Sciences, Natural Sciences, Mathematics, History, and English Composition are not included in the capture; only the Humanities and Fine Arts Group A and Group B lists appear.",
    "The capture labels units as 'Credit Hours' (and once 'Semester Hours'); semester credit system is assumed from that label."
  ],
